  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "Eating out in Hong Kong has its own ritual. You'll hear <em>dim2 sam1</em> (點心 — dim sum, literally 'touch the heart') at yum cha, and the waiter asking <em>jiu3 dim2 je5?</em> ('what would you like?'). Note <strong>lok6 daan1</strong> (落單) for placing an order, and <strong>maai4 daan1</strong> (埋單) for asking for the bill — both are fixed compound verbs worth learning as units. Most everyday eating happens at a <em>caa4 caan1 teng1</em> (茶餐廳 — HK-style cafe).",
